### VirtualizedList
A high-performance scrollable list that renders only visible items, supporting tens of thousands of rows at 60 FPS with minimal memory footprint.

**Import Path**:
```typescript
import { VirtualizedList } from "@/components/ui/virtualizedList/virtualizedList";
```

#### Default
A list of 10,000 items rendered with smooth scrolling. Only visible rows are mounted in the DOM.

```tsx
const items = Array.from({ length: 10000 }, (_, i) => ({
  id: i,
  label: \`Item \${i + 1}\`,
}));

<VirtualizedList
  items={items}
  itemHeight={40}
  height={320}
  renderItem={(item) => (
    <div className="flex items-center px-4 h-full text-sm border-b border-zinc-100 dark:border-zinc-800/50">
      <span className="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-400 w-16">#{item.id + 1}</span>
      <span>{item.label}</span>
    </div>
  )}
/>
```

#### Custom Render
Use the renderItem prop to display complex row layouts with icons, badges, and metadata.

```tsx
const users = Array.from({ length: 5000 }, (_, i) => ({
  id: i,
  name: \`User \${i + 1}\`,
  email: \`user\${i + 1}@example.com\`,
  role: i % 3 === 0 ? "Admin" : i % 3 === 1 ? "Editor" : "Viewer",
}));

<VirtualizedList
  items={users}
  itemHeight={56}
  height={336}
  renderItem={(item) => (
    <div className="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 h-full border-b">
      <Avatar>{item.name.charAt(5)}</Avatar>
      <div className="flex-1 min-w-0">
        <p className="text-sm font-medium truncate">{item.name}</p>
        <p className="text-xs text-zinc-400 truncate">{item.email}</p>
      </div>
      <Badge color={item.role === "Admin" ? "danger" : "default"}>{item.role}</Badge>
    </div>
  )}
/>
```

#### Dynamic Item Height Calculation
Calculate varying row heights dynamically using getItemHeight={(item, index) => number}.

```tsx
<VirtualizedList
  items={items}
  getItemHeight={(item, index) => (index % 2 === 0 ? 44 : 64)}
  height={300}
  renderItem={renderRow}
/>
```

#### Scroll to Index Method
Imperatively jump to any item index in the virtualized list using listRef.current.scrollToIndex(index).

```tsx
const listRef = useRef<VirtualizedListRef>(null);

<button onClick={() => listRef.current?.scrollToIndex(500)}>
  Jump to #501
</button>

<VirtualizedList ref={listRef} items={largeDataset} height={280} />
```

#### Infinite Scroll Loading (onEndReached)
Automatically trigger data fetching when scrolling near bottom threshold with onEndReached.

```tsx
<VirtualizedList
  items={items}
  itemHeight={40}
  height={260}
  onEndReached={() => fetchNextPage()}
/>
```
